.\" Manual page for bedrud(1)
.TH "bedrud" "1" "" "User Commands" "Bedrud"
.SH NAME
bedrud \- self\-hosted video meeting server and operator CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bedrud
[\fIoptions\fR]
.PP
.B bedrud
\fIcommand\fR [\fIsubcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR] [\fIarguments\fR...]
.PP
Common forms:
.PP
.B bedrud
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIfile\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR]
.PP
.B bedrud run
[\fB\-\-skip\-migrate\fR]
.PP
.B bedrud install
[\fIflags\fR...]
.PP
.B bedrud update
\fIsource\fR | \fB\-\-self\fR | \fB\-\-skip\-binary\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bedrud
is a single executable that runs a video meeting API server, serves an
embedded web UI, and can manage an embedded LiveKit WebRTC media server.
It also provides operator commands for installation, upgrades, users,
rooms, configuration, certificates, and database maintenance.
.PP
Invoking management subcommands opens the configuration file and (when
needed) the application database on the host where the server is installed.
.SH OPTIONS
Global options apply to all subcommands unless noted.
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIpath\fR
Path to the configuration YAML file.
Environment:
.BR BEDRUD_CONFIG ,
.BR CONFIG_PATH .
Default for installed systems:
.IR /etc/bedrud/config.yaml .
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine\-readable JSON on stdout for successful operations and errors.
.TP
.B \-h , \-\-help
Show help for a command.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Server
.TP
.B run , server
Start the meeting API server (and related services according to config).
.TP
.B livekit
Start the embedded LiveKit process (legacy/service unit entrypoint).
.SS Installation and lifecycle
.TP
.B install
Create system user and directories, write
.I /etc/bedrud
configuration and LiveKit YAML when those files do not already exist,
install init units, TLS material as requested, example configs under
.IR /usr/share/doc/bedrud/examples/ ,
the manual page, and shell tab\-completion scripts.
Re\-running
.B install
does not overwrite an existing
.I config.yaml
or
.IR livekit.yaml .
Use
.B \-\-fresh
to uninstall first and regenerate them (destroys config and data).
Use
.B update
to replace the binary without touching config.
.TP
.B uninstall
Stop services and remove installed files, configuration, and data
(destructive).
.TP
.B update , upgrade
Upgrade an existing installation.
A source is required: a local binary path, a release archive
(\fB.tar.xz\fR / \fB.tar.gz\fR), an HTTPS URL, the keyword
.BR latest
(GitHub release with checksum verification),
.BR \-\-self
(use the running executable), or
.BR \-\-skip\-binary
(migrations and restart only after a package manager replaced the binary).
.IP
After a successful update, database migrations run (unless skipped),
service units are refreshed, example configs under
.I /usr/share/doc/bedrud/examples/
are rewritten, and the man page plus bash/zsh/fish completions are
refreshed.
.SS Users and rooms
.TP
.B user
Manage accounts (create, delete, list, promote, password, enable/disable, …).
.TP
.B room
Manage rooms (list, info, close, suspend, reactivate, kick).
.SS Configuration and operations
.TP
.B config
Show or modify configuration path/values; validate config.
.TP
.B settings
Show or set runtime settings stored in the database.
.TP
.B certificate , cert
Regenerate, renew, or show TLS certificate information.
.TP
.B invite\-token , invite
Manage registration invite tokens.
.TP
.B db
Run or inspect database migrations.
.TP
.B version
Print the package version.
.SS Shell integration
.TP
.B completion
Print a shell tab\-completion script.
Supported shells:
.BR bash ,
.BR zsh ,
.BR fish .
Redirect to the system completion path (see FILES), or rely on
.B install
/
.B update
to install completions automatically on system installs.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B non\-zero
Invalid usage, missing privileges, configuration error, or command failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BEDRUD_CONFIG , CONFIG_PATH
Override the configuration file path.
.TP
.B SERVER_HTTP_PORT , SERVER_CERT_ALGORITHM , LOG_LEVEL
See configuration documentation; many keys also accept environment overrides.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/bedrud/config.yaml
Primary application configuration (mode 0600 recommended).
.TP
.I /etc/bedrud/livekit.yaml
Embedded LiveKit configuration when not using external LiveKit.
.TP
.I /var/lib/bedrud/
State directory (database, certs, uploads, version file).
.TP
.I /var/log/bedrud/
Log directory when file logging is enabled.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/bedrud/examples/
Example configuration templates.
.TP
.I /usr/share/man/man1/bedrud.1
This manual page (installed by
.B install
/
.BR update ).
.TP
.I /usr/share/bash\-completion/completions/bedrud
Bash completion script.
.TP
.I /usr/share/zsh/site\-functions/_bedrud
Zsh completion script.
.TP
.I /usr/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/bedrud.fish
Fish completion script.
.SH EXAMPLES
Install on a Linux host (interactive when a TTY is present):
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo bedrud install
.RE
.fi
.PP
Upgrade from a downloaded binary:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo bedrud update /tmp/bedrud
.RE
.fi
.PP
Upgrade to the latest stable GitHub release (prompts unless \-y):
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo bedrud update latest
sudo bedrud update latest \-y
.RE
.fi
.PP
List and switch installed versions (\fI/opt/bedrud/versions\fP):
.PP
.nf
.RS
bedrud versions list
bedrud versions list \-\-remote
bedrud versions current
sudo bedrud versions use 1.2.3
sudo bedrud versions prune \-\-keep 5 \-\-yes
sudo bedrud versions remove 1.1.0 \-\-yes
bedrud versions path
.RE
.fi
.PP
Upgrade to the latest nightly/prerelease:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo bedrud update \-\-nightly
sudo bedrud update \-\-nightly \-y
.RE
.fi
.PP
After an apt/dnf package upgrade of the binary only:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo bedrud update \-\-skip\-binary
.RE
.fi
.PP
Install shell completions manually:
.PP
.nf
.RS
bedrud completion bash | sudo tee /usr/share/bash\-completion/completions/bedrud
bedrud completion zsh  | sudo tee /usr/share/zsh/site\-functions/_bedrud
bedrud completion fish | sudo tee /usr/share/fish/vendor_completions.d/bedrud.fish
.RE
.fi
.PP
Read this page after install:
.PP
.nf
.RS
man bedrud
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
Online documentation:
.UR https://bedrud.org/
.UE
and
.UR https://themadorg.github.io/bedrud/
.UE
.PP
Configuration examples on an installed system:
.IR /usr/share/doc/bedrud/examples/ .
